<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The man in black in the set: vanilla's StrangerInBlack (Core
    PawnKindDefs_Humanlikes/PawnKinds_Special.xml), copied field for field since a concrete def
    cannot be a parent, with the gear swapped. Fields not discussed here are vanilla's, labels
    included: the incident's letter names the arrival by its kind label ("a mysterious man in
    black has arrived"), so the labels must stay vanilla's for the letter to read the same.
    Design in Docs/Specs/Man-In-Black.md. Nothing lists this kind: the mod setting writes it
    onto StrangerInBlackJoin's pawnKind (Source/1.6/Settings/Settings_Stranger.cs), and it is
    the only way the kind is reached.

    Gear. apparelRequired is the three pieces, which vanilla's generator adds whatever the
    money, and apparelColor is vanilla's stranger's (0.2, 0.2, 0.2), which
    PawnApparelGenerator.PostProcessApparel paints onto every piece through its CompColorable,
    so the set arrives black with the mask's painted cross and trim kept (the armor def's
    header). ignoreIdeoApparelColors and the Ideology favoriteColor follow vanilla. No
    apparelTags and no apparelMoney: nothing is worn beside a warcasket, and VFEP's own
    generation postfix strips anything else and locks the set on (PawnGenerator_GeneratePawn_Patch).
    weaponTags is MDWC_StrangerInBlack, a tag 1.6/Patches/StrangerInBlackMinigun.xml adds to
    VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketGun_Minigun alone, so the pick is that gun and no other; weaponMoney
    5000 clears its market value (2240) with room for a VFEP repricing, and the tag keeps the
    headroom from buying anything else. itemQuality Good and gearHealthRange 1~1 are vanilla's.

    combatPower 300 is VFEP_Major's, the VFEP raid-table kind closest in gear (a veteran
    warcasket with a veteran gun); a joiner's kind is never costed, so this only matters to a
    mod that lists the kind elsewhere. requiredWorkTags Violent and Caring are vanilla's and
    fit a medic; the Medicine skill range is added beside vanilla's Shooting at the same 8~16,
    so the pilot can use the set he arrives in.

    The gate. The MedicWarcasket.StrangerInBlackExtension (Source/1.6/StrangerInBlack.cs)
    makes a request for this kind generate the fallback, vanilla's StrangerInBlack, while
    VFEP_Warcaskets is unfinished and requiresResearch holds; requiresResearch is a mod setting
    defaulting to this value.

    Other mods' extensions. At startup the fallback's mod extensions are appended to this
    list (StrangerInBlack.MirrorFallbackExtensions), so what a mod attaches to vanilla's
    stranger reaches this kind too: Combat Extended's loadout (the weapon's magazines) and
    Altered Carbon's cortical stack chance. Their patches on vanilla's apparel and weapon do
    not carry over; CE's added backpack would be stripped by VFEP's warcasket postfix anyway.
    No gender is fixed here: vanilla fixes it on the incident (pawnFixedGender Male), and a mod
    setting lifts that.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef>
    <defName>MDWC_StrangerInBlack</defName>
    <label>stranger in black</label>
    <labelMale>man in black</labelMale>
    <labelFemale>woman in black</labelFemale>
    <labelPlural>strangers in black</labelPlural>
    <race>Human</race>
    <defaultFactionDef>OutlanderCivil</defaultFactionDef>
    <combatPower>300</combatPower>
    <minGenerationAge>20</minGenerationAge>
    <maxGenerationAge>55</maxGenerationAge>
    <isFighter>true</isFighter>
    <chemicalAddictionChance>0.05</chemicalAddictionChance>
    <backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>0.05</backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>
    <backstoryFiltersOverride>
      <li>
        <categories>
          <li>Offworld</li>
          <li>Outlander</li>
          <li>Outsider</li>
        </categories>
      </li>
    </backstoryFiltersOverride>
    <requiredWorkTags>
      <li>Violent</li>
      <li>Caring</li>
    </requiredWorkTags>
    <invNutrition>10.0</invNutrition>
    <inventoryOptions>
      <subOptionsChooseOne>
        <li>
          <thingDef>MedicineIndustrial</thingDef>
          <countRange>5</countRange>
        </li>
      </subOptionsChooseOne>
    </inventoryOptions>
    <gearHealthRange>1~1</gearHealthRange>
    <itemQuality>Good</itemQuality>
    <weaponMoney>5000~5000</weaponMoney>
    <weaponTags>
      <li>MDWC_StrangerInBlack</li>
    </weaponTags>
    <apparelRequired>
      <li>MDWC_Warcasket_Medic</li>
      <li>MDWC_WarcasketShoulders_Medic</li>
      <li>MDWC_WarcasketHelmet_Medic</li>
    </apparelRequired>
    <apparelColor>(0.2, 0.2, 0.2)</apparelColor>
    <ignoreIdeoApparelColors>true</ignoreIdeoApparelColors>
    <favoriteColor MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Black</favoriteColor>
    <initialWillRange>0~0</initialWillRange>
    <initialResistanceRange>0~2</initialResistanceRange>
    <humanPregnancyChance>0</humanPregnancyChance>
    <skills>
      <li>
        <skill>Shooting</skill>
        <range>8~16</range>
      </li>
      <li>
        <skill>Medicine</skill>
        <range>8~16</range>
      </li>
    </skills>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="MedicWarcasket.StrangerInBlackExtension">
        <research>VFEP_Warcaskets</research>
        <requiresResearch>true</requiresResearch>
        <fallback>StrangerInBlack</fallback>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </PawnKindDef>
</Defs>
